ec  responds not to worry his power is very  much intact as if that was the only  thing worthy of consideration and for me  the paneling for this fight was honestly  the strongest between chapters 85 and  86. there are some truly great layouts  here that make use of the width and the  height of the page but to bring it back  to the point I like this fight and think  is appropriate because it shows Goku and  Vegeta fighting the physical embodiment  of all their struggles they've had to  overcome on this journey in the ark and  right before our eyes and theirs we see  exactly where that sort of toxic  thinking leads you and just as this  battle Roars onward with gas singing the  upsides of this Choice gorilla makes the  save on Goku and this is where the  conclusion becomes the best ending to a  fight Dragon Ball super has delivered in  my opinion not just because I'm a fan of  the story for all of the reasons I've  mentioned but it also manages to make  use of every single member of the hero  team weak or not without exception to  create the scenario that made for one  heck of a finish granola charges his  finishing attack while Goku defends and  distracts however eventually Goku is  beaten down about to be destroyed Vegeta  throws his body against gas for another  last-ditch effort to draw his attention  away despite Vegeta himself having no  energy at all all the while oil and Maki  are put to sleep by Minato before they  can intervene and just as granola is  about to fire about to finish his charge  Goku's hidden power awakens once again  like he did in the moro Arc to position  gas away from the earth a safe Target  now presents itself and this this is my  favorite part granola's eye eyes are  still suffering from the effects of the  last battle and can't aim correctly  creating the perfect opportunity for  oatmeal the little loyal AI to chime in  and offer his aiming assist Services  culminating in one spectacular final  attack from granola the perfect person  to fire this final blast it's a  breathtaking finish to what has  ultimately been a near brilliantly  structured Arc however with that said I  still want to talk about one other  aspect of it and it revolves around the  implications of bardock's wish made on  the dragon Ball's courtesy of Minato the  wish Bardock makes in chapter 83 speaks  perhaps to a theme echoed in this Arc  one where you shouldn't have your  attention focused on the past where you  shouldn't wish your life away for the  sake of Revenge but to instead cherish  the possibilities the future holes to  cherish what exists now it's a beautiful  sentiment and one that is felt  throughout this Arc to varying degrees  that affects a host of other characters  however my issue with it is divorce from  the Thematic significance which it  definitely has and more so pertains to  the potential implications it might have  for the rest of the series narratively I  spoke about it in an older video closer  to when these chapters came out but the  wording of Braddock's wish whether it be  vis's translation saying he wishes his  children Thrive or whether it be other  accurate translations suggesting he  wished his children to grow up healthy  both run the risk of implying that Goku  didn't survive his childhood years in  early Dragon Ball due to who he was but  instead the wishes of his father  enforced through magic which robs I  think that section that early section of  the story and impact it had for me at  the very least but I do however have  hope and to be honest it more than  likely will be something that will be  addressed by Akira Toriyama eventually  at some point down the road because if  there's one thing I know about Akira  toriyama's writing is that he loves to  keep things vague intentionally Goku  being an alien didn't contradict much of  anything in the original material  because it was kept vague beerus being  the one to give the order to Frieza  doesn't contradict anything really in  the main Canon because again he kept it  vague there are plenty of instances in  this story where Akira Toriyama wrote  the story in such a loose and vague  fashion because he either didn't know  what to write there and then at the time  or intended on expanding upon it later  either way he kept it vague to not write  himself into a corner within which there  would be no return and while this looks  like it could be a potential issue that  might impact the tension and achievement  of Goku from childhood to adulthood it's  also entirely possible that Akira  Toriyama intended for that wearing to  imply the safe passage of Goku from  planet Vegeta to Earth and that from  that point on he'd be on his own it's  impossible to say at this point as he  has left it very vague despite the fact  that there are a number of panels where  Goku and Vegeta seem to address this  aspect and brush it off as a joke and  look whether you value this concern  people have or not whether you like this  decision more than the consequences it  may mean for early Dragon Ball I think  it should be safe to suggest that we all  value you different things about this  series and I hope I communicated those  worries here today well enough for those  that don't agree to potentially  understand and empathize with it to a  certain extent but to close it off I  think we  think was this Arc makes is by  displaying gas as an otherwise very  sympathetic character one whose only  motivation is to do his brother proud  and to not let his family down to prove  himself his worth all the while Alec  isn't concerned with that and whom gas  trusts is willing to slowly watch his  brother Decay away he's despicable I  mean all does is hide behind people at  least Frieza does things first  Frieza is back in the mix baby and I  love him so so much it hurts my body he  gets some quippy lines perfect for his  character he looks terrifying enormously  more powerful thanks to some secret  training in another world or Dimension  making him perhaps now the strongest in  this Dimension and the best part is that  this was sort of foreshadowed in some  respect in chapter 82 where the Oracle  fish after seeing gas doesn't recognize  and peace looks confused at this  Revelation suggesting that he wasn't the  one the fish had visions of suggesting  that he alone wasn't the strongest in  the universe that frees on this and then  Frieza just pieces out leaving everyone  shocked it's perfect I can't wait to see  where Akira Toriyama and toriotaro go  with this uh yeah if you enjoyed this  video be sure to leave a like And  subscribe for more like this but until  then I've been totally not Mark I'll see  you all next weekend thank you so much  for watching it feels good to be back  reviewing Dragon Ball  thank you
 

